result.markdown:
# Model Data Build: Rough & Full Model {.unnumbered}

::: {.lead}
Logistic Regression Modeling
:::




<br>

<br>

::: {.content-hidden when-profile="book"}

Before loading anything, I set R to print numbers in full decimal form instead of scientific notation so the p-values in the coefficient tables are easier to read.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# Print values in decimal form instead of scientific notation.

#== disable attributes ==
# (Andrzej, 2020)
options(
  pillar.sigfig = 5,
  # (Twomey, 2026)
  scipen = 999
)
```
:::


:::

Now, I'll load the packages and the helper utils.R script.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# Load libraries.

#== packages ==
library(gt)
library(here)
library(dplyr)
library(ggplot2)
library(ggpubr)
library(pROC)
library(tidymodels)
library(sessioninfo)
```
:::


::: {.content-hidden when-profile="book"}


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# Source the total_rows function.
# (Buck, 2025; Olumide, 2025)
source(
  here::here(
    "scripts",
    "utils.R"
  )
)
```
:::


I'll also load the modeling dataset produced by the cleaning script.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# Load the homicide modeling dataframe.

#== read modeling Parquet ==
# (Olumide, 2025)
homicide_modeling_df <- arrow::read_parquet(
  here::here(
    "data",
    "processed",
    "homicide_modeling.parquet"
  )
)

#== display records ==
homicide_modeling_df %>%
  head() %>%
  # (Muldoon, 2021)
  gt() %>%
  tab_header(
    title = md("**Homicide Modeling Dataframe**")
  )
```

